From: WinPad
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Log mprotect_exec only now and then.

mprotect_exec logs an ERR line for every protection change it makes
(ml374). FEX's host heap commits its pages through it, so a run of an x86
program logs thousands of

  err:virtual:mprotect_exec mprotect_exec(0x71..., ..., rw-)

that say nothing new after the first few and push the rest of the run out
of the log. It now logs the first 32 calls, then the 64th, 128th, 256th
and so on, each with the running count as "(#N)", so the log still shows
how many there were (tests/fex-wow64/heap-churn.py reads it).

Applies to willfaust/Madeira at 48f9764, after 0001 to 0004. Numbered
0006 because 0005 is taken on another branch (x86-case-lookup, 0005 there
changes dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c only).
---
diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -12399,10 +12399,20 @@ static inline int mprotect_exec( void *base, size_t size, int unix_prot )
      * Apply only on the PROT_WRITE-add path; non-write protect changes go
      * through the regular mprotect below. */
     if (!ios_in_mach_exc)                       /* ml374: see ios_in_mach_exc */
-        ERR("mprotect_exec(%p, 0x%lx, %c%c%c)\n", base, (unsigned long)size,
-            (unix_prot & PROT_READ)  ? 'r' : '-',
-            (unix_prot & PROT_WRITE) ? 'w' : '-',
-            (unix_prot & PROT_EXEC)  ? 'x' : '-');
+    {
+        /* WinPad: the first 32 calls, then every power of two, with the
+         * running count. Every protection change of a process comes through
+         * here (each commit of FEX's host heap pages too), and an ERR line
+         * each is thousands of lines of a run. */
+        static unsigned int mprotect_exec_calls;
+        unsigned int n = ++mprotect_exec_calls;
+
+        if (n <= 32 || !(n & (n - 1)))
+            ERR("mprotect_exec(%p, 0x%lx, %c%c%c) (#%u)\n", base, (unsigned long)size,
+                (unix_prot & PROT_READ)  ? 'r' : '-',
+                (unix_prot & PROT_WRITE) ? 'w' : '-',
+                (unix_prot & PROT_EXEC)  ? 'x' : '-', n);
+    }
     if ((unix_prot & PROT_WRITE) && !(unix_prot & PROT_EXEC))
     {
         /* ml391 (task #60): try WITHOUT VM_PROT_COPY first.  COPY forcibly
